# The .ko-agent-sandbox/egress/allowed of a project that admits its model provider and nothing
# else — the lockdown for a project whose dependency names, or hosts read, are themselves
# secrets. Under --egress=deny-unless-allowed, the default: `-**` removes the baseline, not the
# public HTTPS that allow-unless-denied admits ambiently, so under that profile this file narrows
# nothing. Nothing built in survives: no forge, no registry, no documentation site. The agent
# builds only from what the project directory and the image already hold, and every refusal is a
# line in the proxy log. Change the group to the agent launched: openai for codex, google for agy,
# github for copilot.
-**
+model-provider anthropic
